# What the mobile-gameframe port changes on purpose, and why.
#
# Run it as:
#   gate_diff.py --expect tools/porcelain_gate/expect/mobile-gameframe.expect <pairs...>
#
# One line, and that is the whole of it: six of the seven lanes are byte
# identical, and the seventh differs only in an internal handle. Every rectangle
# of the Stone Drawer -- the housing, the two rail plates, the fourteen rocks,
# their stones and icons, the two switches and their glyphs, the three tap
# blockers, the four filter plates, the torn sheet -- is the number it was, on
# every lane, before and after.
#
# Every line here is a claim a reader is meant to be able to disagree with. If
# you think one of them is wrong, the argument is with the reason, not with the
# tool.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shipped art lands in different image slots on the touch lane.
#
# Every box, every size and every hidden bit of all fifty-seven owned controls
# is identical. What moved is the internal slot number the client hands a
# picture, because the layer now owns when a picture a DESCRIPTION names is
# asked for: it is requested on the describe that first names it instead of all
# sixty-eight at once from on_start, and everything allocated afterwards
# renumbers. The pictures this frame COMPOSES for itself renumber with them --
# fourteen turned stones, two turned plates, the parchment, the chat bar -- for
# the same reason, because they are composed on the describe that first asks
# rather than in one all-or-nothing latch.
#
# THE CLAIM, stated so it can be argued with: a slot id is an internal handle
# and not behaviour. Nothing reads it, nothing persists it, and no two builds
# are obliged to agree on it. This is the same line the gameframe-layout and
# minimap-orbs ports carry, for the same reason, and the same trade is
# available: byte-identity costs keeping every picture resident for the life of
# the client, which is a worse deal than this line on the one machine this
# frame is for.
normalise scene = the image slot is an internal handle, and requesting a picture on the describe that names it renumbers what is allocated after it
